# BlockIQ — Lazra Labs

# Vehicle acquisition intelligence platform for franchised dealer groups

## Stack

- React + Vite + TailwindCSS
- Cloudflare Pages (hosting)
- Cloudflare Workers (API proxy layer — keeps Cox credentials server-side)
- Supabase (session logging, saved filters, dealer profiles)

## Brand

- Navy: #1B2A4A
- Gold: #C5A258
- Font: Plus Jakarta Sans

## Architecture

- All Cox API calls (MMR Valuations, MMR Forecast, Listings Search) go through a Cloudflare Worker proxy — credentials never hit the browser
- Vehicle data is never persisted to Supabase — read-only display only
- Slack webhook for bid approval routing lives in the Worker

## Component structure

src/
components/
FilterBar.jsx # Brand tabs, mileage/CR/MMR sliders, FWD/AS IS toggles
VehicleCard.jsx # VIN, year/make/model, drive, miles, CR badge, MMR, buy target
StatsBar.jsx # Total / survivors / eliminated / avg buy target
BrandProfile.jsx # Per-brand threshold config (INFINITI / Nissan / Volvo / Cadillac / GM)
lib/
cox.js # Cox API calls via Worker fetch
filters.js # Filter logic extracted from current artifact
scoring.js # Green/yellow/red scoring, buy target calc
pages/
Evaluator.jsx # Main run list evaluation view

## Rules

- No Cox API credentials in frontend code ever
- All external API calls go through /api/\* Worker routes
- Filter logic is pure JS — no API calls until survivor list is confirmed
- NHTSA VIN decode runs first to kill FWD before burning MMR API calls
- Supabase RLS scoped by dealership_id (multi-tenant from day one)
